.TH HIER 7
.SH NAME
hier \- the file tree of SIEOS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.TP
.B /bin
the programs; a name typed at the shell runs /bin/NAME. Some are other names
(symbolic links) of one program: passwd, su, useradd, userdel (acct);
ssh-keygen (ssh); rec, vol (play); ping, host, nslookup, ifconfig, netstat,
traceroute, nc, curl, wget (fetch).
.TP
.B /boot
on a USB key, the boot files (loader.efi, kernel.bin, boot.cfg, the boot
modules) the installer copies onto a PC's drive.
.TP
.B /etc
the machine's settings:
.RS
.TP
.BR users ", " groups ", " secrets
the accounts,
.BR users (5)
.TP
.BR hostname ", " motd
the machine's name, the welcome message,
.BR hostname (5)
.TP
.B apps/
everyone's app launchers,
.BR app (5)
.TP
.B ssl/roots
the certificate authorities TLS trusts
.TP
.B ssh/
the SSH server's switch and host key,
.BR authorized_keys (5)
.TP
.BR wifi.conf ", " bluetooth.keys
the Wi-Fi network,
.BR wifi.conf (5);
Bluetooth's bonds (both root only)
.TP
.BR display.conf ", " kblight ", " gfxhat.conf
the screen, the keyboard light, a Pi's GFX HAT
.TP
.BR sia.conf ", " sia.key
the assistant,
.BR sia.conf (5)
.TP
.B boot.log
the log since boot, saved a few times in the first 5 minutes (root only)
.RE
.TP
.B /home/NAME
each user's home, mode 0700, an encrypted volume of its own; dot files
there hold the user's settings
.RB ( ~/.mail ,
.BR ~/.look ,
.BR ~/.mouse ,
.BR ~/.ssh/ ),
and
.B ~/Downloads
takes files received.
.TP
.B /root
root's home.
.TP
.B /lib/sicc
what
.BR cc (1)
builds programs with: headers (include/, include/mk/), the start file, the
library, the linker script.
.TP
.B /lib/fonts
fonts for programs that draw text.
.TP
.B /models
language models (.gguf) for the assistant.
.TP
.B /src
sources SIEOS builds itself: sieos/ (the shell, make, hello and their
Makefile), hello-make/, python/ (examples).
.TP
.B /tmp
for everyone, sticky (mode 1777): a user may not delete other people's
files.
.TP
.B /usr/share/man
these manual pages, one directory per section.
.TP
.B /var/sia
the assistant's conversations, one folder per uid (siad alone).
.TP
.B .snapshots
at the root of every volume, a hidden directory listing its snapshots.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR intro (7),
.BR siefs (5),
.BR snap (1)
